 10 | 	return s
    |  ^^^^^^^^
    |
    = note: `path.last()` reads an element `path` keeps, and what `path` keeps is lent, whether `path` is owned here or borrowed. Giving it away by value would take it out of `path`, and Nikaia never copies behind your back.
    = help: Write `path.last()?.clone()` for a copy.
